---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The Kitchen Calc Terms of Service. Our calculators are free, informational tools for home cooks. Results are estimates — use your own judgment and follow USDA food safety guidelines."
  canonical="https://thekitchencalc.com/terms-of-service/"
>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-secondary mb-6">
      Terms of Service
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-text-light mb-8">
      Last updated: June 2026
    </p>

    <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-border p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-6 text-text-light leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-secondary">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
      <p>
        By accessing and using The Kitchen Calc (thekitchencalc.com), you accept
        and agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you do not agree,
        please do not use the website.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-secondary">2. Description of Service</h2>
      <p>
        The Kitchen Calc provides free, web-based kitchen calculators and meal
        planning tools. All tools are provided "as is" without any warranties,
        express or implied.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-secondary">3. No Professional Advice</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>The calculators on this site are for informational and
        entertainment purposes only.</strong> Results generated by our tools are
        estimates based on standard culinary ratios and publicly available
        guidelines (such as USDA recommendations).
      </p>
      <p>Specifically:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
        <li>Our calculators do <strong>not</strong> constitute professional cooking, nutritional, dietary, or medical advice.</li>
        <li>Scaling recipes — especially for baking — may produce unexpected results due to factors like pan size, ingredient temperature, and atmospheric conditions.</li>
        <li>Always use a food thermometer to verify internal cooking temperatures per USDA guidelines.</li>
        <li>Always follow food safety best practices for handling, cooking, and storing food.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-secondary">4. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, The Kitchen Calc and
        its operators shall not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental,
        special, consequential, or punitive damages arising from your use of,
        or inability to use, the website or its calculators. This includes but
        is not limited to:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
        <li>Food that is undercooked, overcooked, or otherwise unsatisfactory.</li>
        <li>Inaccurate scaling of recipes leading to wasted ingredients.</li>
        <li>Any health or safety issues arising from the use of our calculators.</li>
        <li>Inaccuracies in serving estimates for holiday meals or other events.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-secondary">5. Intellectual Property</h2>
      <p>
        All content on this website, including text, graphics, logos, and
        calculator functionality, is the property of The Kitchen Calc and is
        protected by United States copyright laws. You may not reproduce,
        distribute, or create derivative works without our prior written consent.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-secondary">6. Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        The Kitchen Calc is supported by advertising. We use Google AdSense to
        display advertisements. We are not responsible for the content of
        third-party advertisements or the practices of our advertising partners.
        Please see our Privacy Policy for more information about how advertising
        cookies work.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-secondary">7. Changes to Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We reserve the right to modify these Terms of Service at any time.
        Changes will be effective immediately upon posting to this page. Your
        continued use of the website after any changes constitutes acceptance of
        the new terms.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-secondary">8. Governing Law</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the
        laws of the United States. Any disputes arising from these Terms or your
        use of the website shall be resolved in the courts of the United States.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-secondary">9. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about these Terms of Service, please contact us at
        <strong>legal@thekitchencalc.com</strong>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
